{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#975","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#975","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#975\",\"parent_revision\":\"035625c0b529bcccae6b1a56e6c7bb7a1c42238333b71073fd933ef513bc2fc9\",\"root_revision\":\"035625c0b529bcccae6b1a56e6c7bb7a1c42238333b71073fd933ef513bc2fc9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd TeamCreate dispatch option to /work-milestone alongside the current Agent(isolation: \\\"worktree\\\") dispatch.\\n\\nEvidence: User has a Claude Code session running 10+ hours autonomously on ../vm-flightsimulator, coordinating 60 issues through agent teams. This validates that teams work for sustained parallel execution.\\n\\nCurrent state: work-milestone SKILL.md hardcodes Agent(isolation: \\\"worktree\\\") for all wave dispatch (redesigned in #970 based on the finding that teammates lack the Agent tool).\\n\\nCorrection: Both teammates AND subagents lack the Agent tool \u2014 they have identical tool access. The choice between teams and agents is about inter-worker communication, not capability. Teams add SendMessage for cross-worker coordination which is valuable for long-running milestone sessions.\\n\\nOptions:\\n- --teams flag to select TeamCreate dispatch (teammates communicate via SendMessage)\\n- --agents flag to select Agent(isolation: \\\"worktree\\\") dispatch (independent workers, simpler)\\n- Default: teams (validated by real-world 60-issue session)\\n\\nThe worktree-worker-protocol.md and merge-queue-protocol.md need corresponding updates to support team-based coordination alongside the agent-return model.\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 The validated real-world evidence (10+ hour, 60-issue autonomous session) makes this more than speculative. The current hardcoded kage-bunshin-only path is an artificial constraint. Teams add SendMessage for cross-worker coordination, which is valuable for long-running milestone sessions where items benefit from runtime signaling.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Users who want cross-worker coordination via SendMessage during milestone execution cannot achieve it \u2014 the worktree-only path has no inter-worker communication channel.\\n- Bottleneck: Real-world validated team sessions (vm-flightsimulator, 60 issues, 10+ hours) cannot be replicated via the skill \u2014 the skill hardcodes kage-bunshin, so that workflow lives outside the skill entirely.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Unlocks team-based coordination for long-running milestone sessions where workers benefit from runtime signaling via SendMessage.\\n- Preserves the kage-bunshin path (`--agents`) for users who want simpler, fully isolated, independent workers.\\n- Corrects a false assumption baked into #970 \u2014 that teammates can't orchestrate. Both teammates AND subagents lack the Agent tool; the actual differentiator is SendMessage availability.\\n- Aligns the skill with observed production usage patterns.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `/work-milestone {N}` is invoked with `--teams` (or with no flag, since teams is the default), the milestone orchestrator dispatches each wave item to a team teammate using TeamCreate, enabling SendMessage for cross-worker coordination during the wave.\\n\\nWhen invoked with `--agents`, the orchestrator dispatches via the kage-bunshin spawn script (`spawn.py --worktree`), creating an isolated worktree-backed `claude -p` process per item \u2014 fully independent, no inter-worker communication.\\n\\nIn both modes: the wave structure, merge queue, discovery relay, and quality gate steps are unchanged. The only difference is the worker spawn mechanism and whether SendMessage is available.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nThe `/work-milestone` SKILL.md accepts a `--teams` / `--agents` flag. The dispatch step (Step 5c) branches on the flag:\\n- `--teams` path: uses TeamCreate to spawn one teammate per wave item\\n- `--agents` path: uses the existing kage-bunshin spawn script\\n\\nDefault is `--teams`.\\n\\nThe worktree-worker-protocol.md documents that the worker protocol applies to both dispatch modes, noting that in `--teams` mode workers have SendMessage available. The merge-queue-protocol.md documents both signaling models: Agent-return (agents mode) and SendMessage completion signal (teams mode).\\n\\nThe split between the two protocols should be clearly visible at the decision boundary in the workflow diagram, not distributed across sections.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running `/work-milestone 5 --teams` spawns wave items as TeamCreate teammates (observable: team created, SendMessage available in worker context).\\n2. Running `/work-milestone 5 --agents` spawns wave items via the kage-bunshin `spawn.py --worktree` script (observable: worktree directories created, PIDs tracked).\\n3. Running `/work-milestone 5` (no flag) uses teams dispatch by default (observable: same behavior as `--teams`).\\n4. Both modes complete a full wave cycle: all items dispatched, results collected, branches merged into integration branch.\\n5. The SKILL.md dispatch step (Step 5c) contains a branch on the dispatch mode flag \u2014 it must be observable in the workflow diagram or prose, not implicit.\\n6. `worktree-worker-protocol.md` documents that in `--teams` mode, SendMessage is available; in `--agents` mode, it is not.\\n7. `merge-queue-protocol.md` documents both completion signaling models: Agent-return (agents mode) and SendMessage signal (teams mode).\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:work-milestone \u2014 file: plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/SKILL.md |\\n| Reference | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/references/worktree-worker-protocol.md |\\n| Reference | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-milestone/references/merge-queue-protocol.md |\\n| Prior work | #970 \u2014 Redesign /work-milestone from TeamCreate to worktree agents (closed, verified) \u2014 introduced kage-bunshin dispatch and established the \\\"teammates lack Agent tool\\\" reasoning that this item corrects |\\n| Prior work | #974 \u2014 Add --worktree flag to work-backlog-item and implement-feature (P1, needs-grooming) \u2014 parallel item adding dispatch-mode flag at item level |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 #970 is closed/verified; the kage-bunshin spawn script already exists and is the `--agents` path\\n- Blocks: #974 (--worktree flag on work-backlog-item) \u2014 both items introduce dispatch-mode flags; consistent flag naming and documentation conventions should be agreed before both land\\n- Related: #1061 (--effort flag to kage-bunshin), #1062 (--max-turns cap) \u2014 both affect spawned worker behavior; if --teams mode is added, these flags need to apply to the TeamCreate path too\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 The code change is a conditional branch in one dispatch step. The larger work is updating three documents (SKILL.md workflow diagram, worktree-worker-protocol.md, merge-queue-protocol.md) to cover both dispatch modes without duplicating the shared protocol steps.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **add teamcreate dispatch option to /work-milestone alongside worktree agents** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session 2026-03-21: user reports 10+ hour autonomous team session on vm-flightsimulator coordinating 60 issues successfully\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c45234a0a70c47b69043e406d5ab9cfbbd6b9a4a9121bf8bceccdbc341a120a1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPTE6bQ\"}"}